W AX3051 1491-axtag-trailing-text.ax:6:6-12 restriction-unverifiable "`callIt` claims `restrict(no-recursion)` and the claim cannot be checked: the body CALLS its own parameter `f`, so what it performs is decided by the argument each caller passes - the effect row is complete about this body and says nothing about that call" ?"a limit of the ANALYSIS rather than a defect in the program - AX3037's argument at one remove. There are four readings: an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller and cannot be settled here at all, and - for `no-escape` alone - a region fixpoint that hit its round limit before the facts settled, which is a depth limit rather than anything about this declaration. Name the function at the call, stop calling the parameter, shorten the chain, or drop the claim; `no-cast`, `no-wrap` and `no-trap` are checked regardless, because all three are lexical and need no call resolved"
E AX3138 1491-axtag-trailing-text.ax:6:6-12 axtag-trailing-text "text after the closing `)` of this `;@axiom:` tag is not read: `strict`" #"this text is not read" !"every reader of a tag stops at the last `)`, so a word after it changes nothing the compiler checks; a misspelt `strict` there would silently weaken the claim" ?"move the text inside the parentheses, or onto its own comment line"
E AX3057 1491-axtag-trailing-text.ax:11:6-14 restriction-unproven "`callItOk` claims `restrict(no-recursion, strict)` and the claim cannot be PROVEN: the body CALLS its own parameter `f`, so what it performs is decided by the argument each caller passes - the effect row is complete about this body and says nothing about that call" ?"`strict` asks for a guarantee and not a best effort: where the walk cannot settle the claim, it is refused rather than warned. The four readings are AX3051's - an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller, and a region fixpoint that hit its round limit. Name the function at the call site, stop calling the parameter, shorten the chain, or drop `strict` to keep the claim as a checked best effort (AX3051)"
